><highlight color="#9643FC" opacity="0.399994" creationdate="D:20251013083452+10'00'" flags="print" IT="HighlightNote" date="D:20251013083454+10'00'" name="9b0a3e1b-29f9-40e2-91c6-f335ee7e4a71" page="11" coords="304.440613,745.552246,543.594055,745.552246,304.440613,734.762817,543.594055,734.762817,304.440613,733.590149,543.559631,733.590149,304.440613,722.800720,543.559631,722.800720,304.440613,721.628052,543.566895,721.628052,304.440613,710.838623,543.566895,710.838623,304.440613,709.665955,543.646912,709.665955,304.440613,698.876526,543.646912,698.876526,304.440613,697.760620,543.639587,697.760620,304.440613,686.971191,543.639587,686.971191,304.440613,685.798523,543.557251,685.798523,304.440613,675.009094,543.557251,675.009094,304.440613,673.836426,543.610046,673.836426,304.440613,663.046997,543.610046,663.046997,304.440613,661.874329,543.598511,661.874329,304.440613,651.084900,543.598511,651.084900,304.440613,649.912231,543.647766,649.912231,304.440613,639.122803,543.647766,639.122803,304.440613,637.950134,543.536255,637.950134,304.440613,627.160706,543.536255,627.160706,304.440613,625.988037,543.613770,625.988037,304.440613,615.198608,543.613770,615.198608,304.440613,614.025940,543.635498,614.025940,304.440613,603.236511,543.635498,603.236511,304.440613,602.120605,543.542297,602.120605,304.440613,591.331177,543.542297,591.331177,304.440613,590.158508,543.546265,590.158508,304.440613,579.369080,543.546265,579.369080,304.440613,578.196411,543.548279,578.196411,304.440613,567.406982,543.548279,567.406982,304.440613,566.234314,504.844116,566.234314,304.440613,555.444885,504.844116,555.444885" rect="304.103455,555.107727,543.984924,745.889404" subject="Comment on Text" title="alexd"
><contents-richtext
><body xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" xmlns:xfa="http://www.xfa.org/schema/xfa-data/1.0/" xfa:APIVersion="Acrobat:25.1.0" xfa:spec="2.0.2"
><p dir="ltr"
><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:-14.0pt;text-align:left;color:#000000;font-weight:normal;font-style:normal"
>Q14c: </span
><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:-13.3pt;text-align:left;color:#000000;font-weight:normal;font-style:normal"
>Although the current data provide insights into the development&#xD;of cycling-specific guidelines, the partitional calorimetry&#xD;calculations are limited by the estimations of oxygen uptake,&#xD;the respiratory exchange ratio, skin temperature, and skin&#xD;wettedness (i.e., heat acclimation status). As such, additional&#xD;research with individualized athlete data is required to provide&#xD;empirically derived thresholds for stage/race modification&#xD;based on the dynamic balance between endogenous heat production&#xD;and heat exchange with the surrounding environment.&#xD;In cycling, particular attention should also be placed on total&#xD;ascent or course profile because of its effect on increasing&#xD;work rate and reducing heat exchange. Additional research is&#xD;also warranted in female athletes to determine if sex differences&#xD;in sudomotor function (i.e., lower sweat gland output)&#xD;at elevated requirements for heat loss relative to males (58) require&#xD;the development of sex-specific heat policies.</span
></p
></body
></contents-richtext
><popup flags="print,nozoom,norotate" open="no" page="11" rect="584.956970,653.552246,768.956970,745.552246"
/></highlight
